{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"heat transfer in solids and fluids interface heat transfer in solids and fluids interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md","fileName":"Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","Conjugate Heat Transfer Coupling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"heat transfer in solids and fluids interface heat transfer in solids and fluids interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md","fileName":"Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface","heading":"Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A heat-transfer interface spanning solids and fluids uses conduction in every participating domain and adds fluid energy transport where motion exists. Domain-specific material properties and sources enter one shared temperature formulation.\n\nUsed alone, the interface can approximate a fluid as a conducting domain or accept prescribed velocity information. Coupling it to a flow interface creates [[Conjugate Heat Transfer Coupling|conjugate heat transfer]] in which velocity and temperature are solved consistently.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","Conjugate Heat Transfer Coupling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"heat transfer in solids and fluids interface heat transfer in solids and fluids interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md","fileName":"Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Heat Transfer in Solids and Fluids Interface","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","Conjugate Heat Transfer Coupling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}